      "side": 1,
      "message": "Non-wildcard cookie domain incorrectly matches subdomains.\n\nThe comment says \"Support exact match and wildcard (leading dot) domains\", but the current logic applies the `endswith` check unconditionally — regardless of whether the cookie domain has a leading dot. This means a cookie entry like `my-gerrit.com` (no leading dot) will also match `sub.my-gerrit.com`, which contradicts the stated intent.\n\nThe fix is to only apply the `endswith` check when the original `cookie_domain` had a leading dot:\n```suggestion\n                    # Support exact match and wildcard (leading dot) domains.\n                    if cookie_domain.startswith(\".\"):\n                        normalized \u003d cookie_domain.lstrip(\".\")\n                        match \u003d domain \u003d\u003d normalized or domain.endswith(\".\" + normalized)\n                    else:\n                        match \u003d domain \u003d\u003d cookie_domain\n                    if match:\n```",
